leted":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Ensure stubs packages are not installed\n\n- [X] No sqlalchemy stub packages is installed (both `sqlalchemy-stubs` and `sqlalchemy2-stubs` are not compatible with v2)\n\n### Verify if the api is typed\n\n- [X] The api is not in a module listed in [#6810](https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/6810) so it should pass type checking\n\n### Describe the typing issue\n\n`Values().data(...)` works only if my tuples are exact `Tuple[Any, ...]` because `List` is invariant.\n\n### To Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom collections.abc import Sequence\r\nfrom typing import Any\r\n\r\nimport sqlalchemy as sa\r\n\r\ndef variant(_: Sequence[tuple[Any, ...]]) -> None:\r\n    ...\r\n\r\n\r\ndef invariant(_: list[tuple[Any, ...]]) -> None:\r\n    ...\r\n\r\n\r\na: tuple[int, int] = (1, 1)\r\nb: list[tuple[int, int]] = [(1, 1)]\r\n\r\nvariant([a])\r\nvariant(b)\r\n\r\ninvariant([a])\r\ninvariant(b)\r\n\r\n\r\ndata: list[tuple[int, str]] = [(1, \"name1\"), (2, \"name2\"), (3, \"name3\")]\r\n\r\nvalue_expr = sa.values(\r\n    sa.column(\"id\", sa.Integer), sa.column(\"name\", sa.String), name=\"my_values\"\r\n).data(data)\n```\n\n\n### Error\n\n```\r\na.py:21: error: Argument 1 to \"invariant\" has incompatible type \"list[tuple[int, int]]\"; expected \"list[tuple[Any, ...]]\"  [arg-type]\r\na.py:21: note: \"List\" is invariant -- see https://mypy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/common_issues.html#variance\r\na.py:21: note: Consider using \"Sequence\" instead, which is covariant\r\na.py:28: error: Argument 1 to \"data\" of \"Values\" has incompatible type \"list[tuple[int, str]]\"; expected \"list[tuple[Any, ...]]\"  [arg-type]\r\na.py:28: note: \"List\" is invariant -- see https://mypy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/common_issues.html#variance\r\na.py:28: note: Consider using \"Sequence\" instead, which is covariant\r\n``` \n\n### Versions\n\n- OS: Ubuntu\r\n- Python: 3.11\r\n- SQLAlchemy: 2.0.19\r\n- Type checker (eg: mypy 0.991, pyright 1.1.290, etc): mypy 1.5.1\r\n\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/10451/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/10451/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}